---
title: Quickstart
description: Register an OAuth client, request scopes, and exchange your first token in about five minutes.
---

This guide takes you from zero to a working access token. You'll register a client,
run the authorization-code flow with PKCE, and make an authenticated request.

## 1. Register a client

Create an OAuth client from the NeoWorks dashboard, or via the API:

```http
POST /oauth/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "My App",
  "redirect_uris": ["https://myapp.dev/callback"],
  "scopes": ["contacts:read", "tasks:write"]
}
```

You receive a `client_id`. Public clients (SPAs, native apps) use PKCE and never need a
secret.

## 2. Send the user to authorize

Redirect the user to the authorization endpoint with a PKCE challenge:

```
GET /oauth/authorize
  ?response_type=code
  &client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
  &redirect_uri=https://myapp.dev/callback
  &scope=contacts:read tasks:write
  &code_challenge=BASE64URL(SHA256(verifier))
  &code_challenge_method=S256
```

After the user consents, they are redirected back with a `code`.

## 3. Exchange the code for a token

```http
POST /oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code
&code=THE_CODE
&redirect_uri=https://myapp.dev/callback
&client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID
&code_verifier=THE_VERIFIER
```

The response contains a scoped JWT:

```json
{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 3600
}
```

## 4. Make an authenticated request

Send the token as a bearer credential. Scope violations are rejected at the database
layer, so you only ever see data the user granted you.

```http
GET /v1/contacts
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOi...
```

## Where to go next

- The full [OAuth guide](/docs/neoworks/oauth) covers refresh tokens, JWKS, and offline verification.
- Run the whole stack locally with [Self-hosting](/docs/neoworks/self-host).
